1
00:05:15,789 --> 00:05:21,789
Forgotten but not gone.

2
00:10:31,578 --> 00:10:37,578
Blue Moon is a history, drama, comedy film directed by Richard Linklater.

3
00:15:47,368 --> 00:15:53,368
On the evening of March 31, 1943, legendary lyricist Lorenz Hart confronts his shattered self-confidence in Sardi’s bar as his
former collaborator Richard Rodgers celebrates the opening night of his ground-breaking hit musical “Oklahoma!”.

4
00:21:03,157 --> 00:21:09,157
Lorenz Hart, played by Ethan Hawke.

5
00:26:18,947 --> 00:26:24,947
Elizabeth Weiland, played by Margaret Qualley.

6
00:31:34,736 --> 00:31:40,736
Eddie, played by Bobby Cannavale.

7
00:36:50,526 --> 00:36:56,526
Richard Rodgers, played by Andrew Scott.

8
00:42:06,315 --> 00:42:12,315
Morty Rifkin, played by Jonah Lees.

9
00:47:22,105 --> 00:47:28,105
Oscar Hammerstein II, played by Simon Delaney.

10
00:52:37,894 --> 00:52:43,894
Blue Moon is a 2025 American biographical comedy-drama film directed by Richard Linklater and written by
Robert Kaplow, reportedly inspired by the letters of Elizabeth Weiland to Lorenz Hart.

11
00:57:53,684 --> 00:57:59,684
The film stars Ethan Hawke, Margaret Qualley, Bobby Cannavale and Andrew Scott.

12
01:03:09,473 --> 01:03:15,473
Its plot follows Hart as he reflects on himself on the opening night of
Oklahoma!, a new musical by his former colleague Richard Rodgers.

13
01:08:25,263 --> 01:08:31,263
Blue Moon had its world premiere at the main competition of the 75th Berlin International Film Festival on
February 18, 2025, where it won the Silver Bear for Best Supporting Performance for Scott.

14
01:13:41,052 --> 01:13:47,052
At the 83rd Golden Globe Awards, it was nominated for Best Motion
Picture – Musical or Comedy and Best Actor for Hawke.

15
01:18:56,842 --> 01:19:02,842
At the 98th Academy Awards, Kaplow was nominated for Best
Original Screenplay and Hawke for Best Actor.

16
01:24:12,631 --> 01:24:18,631
It was theatrically released in the United States by Sony Pictures Classics on
October 17, 2025, and received positive reviews from critics.

17
01:29:28,421 --> 01:29:34,421
The film explores themes of lyricist, 1940s, intimate, egotistical, admiring.

18
01:34:44,210 --> 01:34:50,210
The tone is lighthearted and emotional.
